      "content": "It is much more effective to frame these viewpoints as a necessary tension rather than presenting them as binary opposites, as acknowledging the role of individual agency within structural constraints deepens students' critical thinking. You can introduce the concept of **agency within structure**, helping students understand how personal choices both reinforce and challenge large-scale systems without erasing the power of those structures. For instance, discuss how moving against the odds is still harder when facing systemic barriers, which validates personal effort while contextualizing institutional hurdles. This balanced approach encourages students to analyze how their decisions fit into a larger historical and social landscape.",
